QuestGuidance.Register("en",86,{
[2721]="7002A828\n1\tDefeat Dargnákh using the sun's rays\tUse the sun to defeat Dargnákh.\n",
[2722]="70028B8E\n1\tDefeat Draigoch after fully weakening him\tDragons are powerful and proud creatures.\n",
[2723]="7001E5E2\n1\tDefeat Dúnlang\tDúnlang was given the power to enslave weaker minds, and many of the Eglain have gone missing over the years. He makes his home deep within the ruins of the Garth Agarwen Fortress and is in the process of converting members of the Eglain into devoted members of the Créoth clan. You should save them from the influence of this man, but not harm them in the process. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2724]="7001E684\n1\tDefeat Ergoth\tYou should defeat the morroval-queen, Ergoth while she is at her strongest. If you weaken her first, you will not be able to claim the greatest of rewards.\n",
[2725]="7002497C\n1\tReach the final confrontation with fear\tConfront your fear. When the moment comes, do not turn your back on it.\n2\tDefeat Durin's Bane\tDo not turn your back on your fear. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2726]="70045222\n1\tDefeat the Princes of Harad\tYou must defeat the Princes of Harad without slaying a single ally that comes to their aid. The sons of the Black Serpent are the pride of Harad, and seeing them slain would demoralize all that fight alongside them. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2727]="7002BBD6\n1\tSave Fangorn from Saruman's army\tWhile protecting Fangorn from Saruman's forces, you must not let any of the Ents die. These ancient tree-herders must survive at all costs.\n",
[2728]="700459BC\n1\tConfront Vadokhar\tVadokhar feeds on flame and shadow, drawing vile strength from both. You must defeat him without allowing him to gather the power of more than one type.\n2\tDefeat Vadokhar without allowing him to consume more than one type of fell power\tVadokhar feeds on flame and shadow, drawing vile strength from both. You must defeat him without allowing him to gather the power of more than one type. Note: You must either defeat him while allowing him to gather only Fire or only Shadow within the encounter. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2729]="7002A70B\n1\tFind the bearers of the Rings of Fire and Frost\tYou must find the bearers of the Rings of Fire and Frost.\n2\tDefeat the giants\tBoth Dunlending giants must be defeated when they have zero Gathered Rage. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2730]="700223B7\n1\tReach the North Annex\tThe greatest of the school's knowledge is kept within the north annex.\n2\tExtinguish the bookstands (total: 10)\tThe School at Tham Mirdaín did not contain much of the knowledge that the library did, but there were several tomes of great import. The forces here have learned all they can and are now burning the books to keep the information from the hands of the Free Peoples. The books must be saved.\n3\tDefeat Commander Târsh\tThe books are safe for the moment, but the forces here will likely attempt to destroy them again if they are allowed the opportunity.\n",
[2731]="700595ED\n1\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers.\n2\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers.\n",
[2732]="700595F0\n1\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers.\n2\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers\tComplete 'Bee's Big Business' without losing any flowers.\n",
[2733]="70022B2F\n1\tApproach Gaerdring and Gaerthel\tGaerdring and Gaerthel, ancient warrior brothers, have arisen deep within the maze of the Great Barrow.\n2\tDefeat Crawling Arms (total: 20)\tGaerthel will enter the battle early if sufficiently taunted. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat Gaerdring\030Defeat Gaerthel\tDefeat the brothers together. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2734]="7001E687\n1\tFil Gashan is far to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall, and General Talug can be found in the depths of that place. Sigurd has challenged you to use stealth and wit to conquer General Talug, the leader of a great Orc-host, without defeating too many of his sentries.\t\n",
[2735]="7001CD58\n1\tDefeat Grimbark, but do not destroy the beehives\tThe Huorn Grimbark is lost to the corruption that has long plagued this land. It is an unfortunate end for a once noble creature, but Grimbark cannot be redeemed. You are tasked with destroying Grimbark, but you should avoid harming the bees under his dominion.\n",
[2736]="70022578\n1\tDestroy all of the Ice-drake hatchlings\tEvery drake egg and Ice-drake hatchling within Grisgart's chamber must be destroyed. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2737]="7001E686\n1\tDefeat the Gurvand\tThe region of the Dark Delvings is far to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. The dwarf Sigurd has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat the Gurvand without the help of runes, wishing you to prove your worth as the great warrior you are rumoured to be. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2738]="7004356B\n1\tComplete 'The Ruined City' without defeating Palace of Eldacar harrowing spirits\tThe mysterious figure remains ever one step ahead... and any hope of finding Faramir at last with it.\n2\tComplete 'The Ruined City' without defeating Palace of Eldacar harrowing spirits\tThe mysterious figure has been revealed to be the Ranger Lúmithil, stabbed with a Morgul-blade and changed into a Cargûl. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2739]="7001E68B\n1\tDefeat Hwandrin\tHwandrin and her brood ever belch unwholesome filth upon the corpse-ridden halls of Skûmfil, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. Sigurd has challenged you to defeat Hwandrin in Skûmfil as proof of your worth as a warrior. Her threat is great, yet few are wilful enough to withstand the menace of such an old and malevolent being.\n",
[2740]="7001E689\n1\tDefeat Igash\tMany tribes of Orcs prowl the Grand Stair, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. Geirr has asked you to defeat Igash in the Grand Stair without defeating any other members of the Moria Orc-tribes. In doing so, you will assist in efforts to reclaim that cross-roads for the dwarves and prove your great worth to Sigurd.\n",
[2741]="7002D568\n1\tApproach Brogadan\tFind Brogadan, Wraith of Fire, in the third tower of Fornost.\n2\tAllow the room to be engulfed in fire\tBrogadan, Wraith of Fire, is master over flames. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat Brogadan\tBrogadan, Wraith of Fire, is ready to meet his final end.\n",
[2742]="7001D019\n1\tDefeat Ivar the Blood-hand without destroying his banners\tIvar the Blood-hand must fall. His strength must fade, and he must become what he should have been all along: a memory of a bygone age. His strength is born of raising the Dead and returning those that have fallen back to battle. This is his role, and stopping him from achieving this role, no matter how minutely, will see that the mark of his hand is removed from the land. To do this, you must ensure that his banners remain so that at his death his power is split between them.\n",
[2743]="7004C02A\n1\tKhílnat, the Silent Shade will appear somewhere in Seregost if her brood is in need. You should defeat Khílnat, the Silent Shade.\t\n",
[2744]="7001E688\n1\tDefeat Narkû to alert Kranklûk of your presence\tThe Forges of Khazad-dûm are to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall. The dwarf Sigurd has challenged you to fight your way to the Orc Kranklûk. Narkû, who stands between you and your intended quarry, will undoubtedly alert Kranklûk that you are coming. You will have a limited amount of time in which to accomplish your task after the warning goes out.\n2\tDefeat Kranklûk before the time runs out\tKranklûk is in the heart of the Forges of Khazad-Dûm. Narkû has been defeated, and Kranklûk is alerted to your presence. Sigurd believes that Kranklûk is the driving force in the Forges of Khazad-dûm; he wants you to defeat your foe to hinder the efforts of the Orcs. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2745]="70044F25\n1\tDefeat Kálmok and his squadron of Trolls in quick succession\tKálmok and his squadron of Trolls hold the southern gate of the Rammas Echor. All must be defeated in quick succession if Aragorn's army is to arrive upon the battlefield with haste.\n2\tDefeat Kálmok and his squadron of Trolls in quick succession\tKálmok and his squadron of Trolls hold the southern gate of the Rammas Echor. All must be defeated in quick succession if Aragorn's army is to arrive upon the battlefield with haste. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tComplete the Quays of the Harlond instance\tComplete the Quays of the Harlond instance.\n",
[2746]="70024975\n1\tOpen the gates forward\tTo begin, you must open the path forward. Once open, be prepared to aggressively move forward.\n2\tDefeat the mammoth-riders\tThe mammoths must be brought to the end of the paths and then defeated. Do this as quickly as possible in order to show Gortheron you are a force to be reckoned with. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2747]="7002D5D4\n1\tApproach Remmenaeg\tRemmenaeg is in the final tower of Fornost.\n2\tDefeat Remmenaeg\tRemmenaeg must be defeated without lighting the braziers too many times. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2748]="70036F82\n1\tChallenge: Dethrone Thane Rípmaush\tRípmaush can be found in the Mead Hall of Marton, sitting upon the Thane's chair and surrounded by his minions. You should dethrone Rípmaush, the false Thane.\n2\tChallenge: Dethrone Thane Rípmaush\tRípmaush can be found in the Mead Hall of Marton, sitting upon the Thane's chair and surrounded by his minions. You should dethrone Thane Rípmaush.\n3\tCompleted\tRípmaush has been removed from the Thane's chair of Marton's Mead Hall.\n",
[2749]="7001EEF9\n1\tClear the pens of all meat-slabs\tThe slavering Wargs reside in the Warg-pens of Dol Guldur. You must goad the Wargs to consume all the slabs of vile meat located throughout the encounter, then attempt to best them in their strengthened state.\n",
[2750]="7001E5E3\n1\tAid in the cleansing of the Red-maid\tThe Créoth will sacrifice themselves to the Red-maid to restore her strength and connexion to the corruption within the swamp. These Men deserve nothing better than death, and your presence in standing against the Red-maid may alert some part of her to the folly of her ways. You should let these Men die and strengthen the Red-maid, then defeat her. Perhaps a piece of her will understand that the corruption has grown too great, and she must return to the natural world which she was once part of. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2751]="7002247C\n1\tBegin the battle with Nengon\tNengon resides at the far end of the gardens.\n2\tDefeat Nengon and his brethren\tNengon and his darkwater brethren must all be defeated in rapid succession, lest they are allowed a chance to recover and reform.\n3\tDefeat Nengon and his brethren\tNengon and his darkwater brethren must all be defeated in rapid succession, lest they are allowed a chance to recover and reform. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2752]="70043535\n1\tThe Black Blade of Lebennin, along with the Witch-king of Angmar and four of his brethren, oversee the Morgul-host in Osgiliath. All but the Witch-king patrol the city atop their winged fell-beasts - powerful allies to Sauron's servants.\t\n",
})
